[asy]
pair P,Q,R,SS,T;
Q = (0,0);
R = (1,0);
P = (0.8,0.5);
SS = 0.6*P;
T = R + 0.6*(P-R);
draw(T--SS--P--R--Q--SS);
label("$P$",P,N);
label("$S$",SS,NW);
label("$Q$",Q,S);
label("$R$",R,S);
label("$T$",T,ENE);
[/asy]

If the measure of $\angle TSQ$ is $145^{\circ}$, then the measure of $\angle TSP$ is $180^\circ - 145^\circ = 35^{\circ}$ since they are supplementary angles. The measure of $\angle RQP$ is also $35^{\circ}$ since sides $TS$ and $RQ$ are parallel. Now we have two of the three angles in triangle $PQR$. To find the third, we calculate $180^{\circ} - 65^{\circ} - 35^{\circ} = 80^{\circ}$. The measure of $\angle PRQ$ is $\boxed{80^{\circ}}$.

